        "surveyID": "109923",
        "narrative": "<p>THE LAKE TROUT POPULATION APPEARS TO HAVE VIRTUALY DISAPPEARED SINCE 1972. WALLEYE NUMBERS ARE ABOUT AVG FOR THE REGION, BUT THERE APPEARS TO BE ONLY A LIMITED NUMBER OF AGE CLASSES PRESENT. GROWTH RATES ARE GOOD, PROBABLY DUE TO THE HIGH QUALITY DWARF CISCO FORAGE BASE. AGING INDICATES MOST CISCO ARE IN TEH I AND II YEAR CLASS, AND ARE SHOWING GOOD GROWTH, HOWEVER, IT APPEARS THERE IS NO GROWTH AFTER AGE III. THERE ARE LARGE NUMBERS OF WHITEFISH PRESENT, PROBABLY ENOUGH TO SUPPORT SOME COMMERCIAL OR SPORT NETTING. SMALLMOUTH BASS ARE PRESENT BUT WERE NOT TAKEN IN THIS ASSESSMENT.</p>"
